# dsv41: two fixes to the pinned engine and the patches before this one.
# - A prompt pass drops the Engram read-ahead an earlier pass left. fillChunk takes a joined read-ahead whose
#   (ahead_start, ahead_n) match its chunk; a pass that ends between two chunks (a cancel or an error) leaves one
#   standing, and a later prompt resuming a kept state at exactly that position (in memory, or restored from disk once
#   the spill tier is on) took rows hashed from the other prompt's ids: wrong Engram rows, and no error. fillBegin now
#   calls the new Model.resetEngramAhead (joinAhead, then the read-ahead's ready flags, count and error cleared) at the
#   start of every pass, so each chunk reads its own rows. Found while porting spill v2's kept state.
# - 0010's timer-slack prctl runs on Linux only, so the dsv41 module's host tests also build on macOS (rdma.zig).
# No switch (always on). A pass reads the rows an unbroken pass reads, so replies are unchanged: exact.py identical to
# the daily baseline on the pair with the fix in (every run since the round-1 engine, 31/31 there, 39/39 later).
# By Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo). Apache-2.0.

Rebased onto TensorFold fbbc971 (28-oct-2026): upstream's fillBegin resets the read-ahead marks (and the Engram lead's) without joining; resetEngramAhead joins first and does both, and fillBegin calls it.

